.TH WSA 1 "2026-11-04" "wsa 3.1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wsa \- Wireless Security Assessment Framework
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wsa
[\fB\-\-auto\fR]
[\fB\-\-wordlist\fR \fIPATH\fR | \fB\-\-mask\fR \fIMASK\fR]
.br
.B wsa
\fB\-\-role=\fINAME\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wsa
is a tmux-based wireless security assessment conductor for OPEN, WEP,
WPA-Personal, WPA3, and WPA-Enterprise networks. It drives aircrack-ng,
hostapd-mana, hashcat, and john from a single terminal UI and produces
NIST SP 800-53 remediation reports.
.PP
It is intended for two audiences: students (methodology text, references,
and teaching-grade walkthroughs for each protocol) and practitioners
(structured capture, filter, and recovery pipeline with a plain-text
assessment report ready to hand to a reviewer).
.PP
.BR wsa " must be run as root:"
wireless operations require
.B CAP_NET_ADMIN
and raw socket access.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-auto
Run an automated assessment. Worker panes deploy normally (real-time
traffic is visible), but the conductor signals each step automatically.
If neither
.B \-\-wordlist
nor
.B \-\-mask
is supplied, capture-only mode is used.
.TP
.BI \-\-wordlist " PATH"
Use a dictionary wordlist as the recovery strategy. Implies
.BR \-\-auto .
.TP
.BI \-\-mask " MASK"
Use a hashcat-style mask as the recovery strategy. Tokens:
.BR ?l " (lower),"
.BR ?u " (upper),"
.BR ?d " (digit),"
.BR ?s " (special),"
.BR ?a " (all),"
.BR ?1..?9 " (custom charsets)."
Implies
.BR \-\-auto .
.TP
.BI \-\-role= NAME
Internal use. Worker panes re-exec the engine with
.BR \-\-role=<name> .
Valid names:
.BR capture ,
.BR mac ,
.BR ping ,
.BR deauth ,
.BR fakeauth ,
.BR arpreplay ,
.BR evil_twin_personal ,
.BR evil_twin_enterprise ,
.BR analyse .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B sudo python3 wsa.py
Launch the interactive manual conductor.
.TP
.B sudo python3 wsa.py \-\-auto \-\-mask '?d?d?d?d?d?d?d?d'
Automated assessment using an 8-digit numeric mask.
.TP
.B sudo python3 wsa.py \-\-auto \-\-wordlist /usr/share/wordlists/rockyou.txt
Automated assessment using a dictionary wordlist.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/wsa/settings.json
Persisted settings (adapters, themes, wordlist folder, thresholds).
.TP
.I .wsa_current
Pointer to the active assessment folder.
.TP
.I assessments/<essid>/
Per-target evidence and reports.
.TP
.I /tmp/wsa_debug.log
Conductor debug trace (useful for support).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SUDO_USER
When invoked under sudo, WSA uses this to determine the correct user
for file ownership of assessment folders and reports.
.SH NOTES
WEP recovery requires approximately 50,000 IVs for reliable PTW
recovery. The failure card reports how many IVs were actually collected
so the operator can re-run capture for longer.
.PP
The analysis console filters rogue-side handshakes (those that crack
with the fake rogue PSK) out of subsequent attacks, so mask and
wordlist runs only test material that can produce a real target
recovery.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aircrack-ng (1),
.BR hashcat (1),
.BR john (1),
.BR hostapd (8),
.BR tmux (1)
